; AlifePlus outpost stock policy. Filters a conquered-area service NPC's player-facing stock
; after each restock, so a field outpost sells a lean assortment instead of the full faction
; shelf. Applied on top of the below-hub supplies drop (Mutators > Conquest); this file decides
; WHICH kinds a service stocks, the supplies drop decides HOW DEEP its ammo/gear tiers go.
;
; ONE BLOCK PER SERVICE ROLE. A cap that suits a trader guts a specialist: a barman's whole trade
; is food and drink, a medic's is medical, a mechanic's is tools and parts. Each role is capped
; generously in its own trade and hard everywhere else, so a service stays recognisably itself.
; A role whose block is missing or empty is not filtered at all (logged at load).
;
; FORMAT: `key = N`. One number, a CAP. There is no minimum: nothing here ever adds stock, it
; only removes what is over the cap.
;   N = 0  -> stripped from stock entirely.
;   N > 0  -> kept, capped at N.
;   row deleted entirely -> that category is left untouched.
; DLTX-overridable.
;
; HOW A ROW COUNTS -- read the key name:
;   <category>              a SHELF TOTAL for that whole category. `food = 8` means 8 food items
;                           on the shelf, all kinds together. Vanilla lists many sections per
;                           category (a barman's supply list carries 77 separate meats and foods),
;                           so a total is the only cap that keeps the shelf lean.
;   ammo_rounds_per_type    ROUNDS, not boxes, and counted separately for each ammo type. 90 means
;                           90 rounds of EACH type, so a shelf carries several calibers and ammo
;                           stays the bulk of a trader's business. A box counts as the rounds in
;                           it, so a value below one box size (30-60 rounds for most types) strips
;                           that ammo entirely rather than leaving a partial box -- stacks release
;                           whole.
;   <item section>          a row may also name one item section (energy_drink = 2); it then caps
;                           that section alone and overrides its category row.
;
; Category names match get_section_category (the same vocabulary the other policy files use).
; Equipped weapon and armor and quest items are never in scope -- the categorizer skips them.

; Field resupply post: ammo by the caseload plus a little of everything else.
[ap_outpost_stock_trader]
ammo_rounds_per_type = 60
grenade_ammo         = 2
grenade              = 2
medkit               = 2
bandage              = 4
antirad              = 2
stim                 = 2
pill                 = 2
food                 = 5
drink                = 4
crafting             = 4
weapon               = 0
outfit               = 0
helmet               = 0
artefact             = 0
device               = 0
other                = 0

